    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d461">

                <pb facs="0723" n="607" xml:id="pg607"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.113/445: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-03-02T17:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 2, 1923—5
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 2—9:22
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>71. Is President’s proclamation of March 4, 1922,<anchor n="34" xml:id="d461-f1"
                    /> regarding export arms and ammunition of war from the United States to China
                    applicable to the Philippine Islands?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
